        "content": "```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Login Form</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n    form {\n      background-color: #f1f1f1f1;\n      padding: 20px;\n      margin: auto;\n      width: 30%;\n      max-width: 400px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h2>Login Form</h2>\n  <form action=\"/login\" method=\"post\">\n    <label for=\"username\">Username:</label><br>\n    <input type=\"text\" id=\"username\" name=\"username\" required><br>\n    <label for=\"password\">Password:</label><br>\n    <input type=\"password\" id=\"password\" name=\"password\" required><br>\n    <button type=\"submit\">Login</button>\n  </form>\n</body>\n```\n```javascript\n// Server-side code (Node.js)\nconst express = require('express');\nconst bodyParser = require('body-parser');\nconst app = express();\napp.use(bodyParser.urlencoded({ extended: true });\n\napp.post('/login', (req, res) => {\n  const username = req.body.username;\n  const password = req.body.password;\n\n  // Validate input and authenticate user with database\n  //\n});\n```\nThis is a basic login form using HTML and Angular that allows users to enter their credentials and submit them to the server for authentication. To make it more secure, you can implement input validation on the client-side using Angular Forms, sanitize user-generated content, use prepared statements in your database queries to prevent SQL injection, and use strong passwords and limit access to sensitive data. You should also regularly update your software, libraries, and frameworks, keep your servers up-to-date with the latest security patches, monitor for vulnerabilities, and implement Content Security Policy (CSP) to prevent XSS attacks."
